{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1354653-who-were-your-first-characters","id":1354653,"title":"Who were your first characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-12T13:03:07-08:00","id":1354653,"title":"Who were your first characters?","content":"In my quest to finally learn how Third Edition works, I'm updating my first two Exalted characters for the new system. I have a lot of fond memories of these two, so it got me curious about what everyone else's early experiences with the game were like. Tell me a bit out your first characters. <br /> <br /> My very first character, back in 2005 during the waning days of 1st Edition, was <b>Ellario Last-of-Faith</b>. He was a Zenith, who exalted when the local authorities purged the little cult he belonged to. This cult believed that pain was necessary to purge impurities from the soul, and it was Ellario's duty to perform the purification rituals. He wielded a dagger that inflicted more pain than damage. He had become so desensitized to pain that only his own dagger could inflict any on him (all his health boxes were -0's unless someone turned the dagger against them, then they became -4's). I maxed out on Ox Body Techniques during character creation so I wouldn't have to learn a bunch of Charms immediately. The rest were mostly Melee Charms. Ellario didn't last long in the game, as he soon discovered that founder of his cult was a Deathlord who promised to aid him in avenging them. So he went over to the other side and became an NPC antagonist.<br /> <br /> My second character was <b>Heart-Melts-As-Snow</b>, a demonlogist from the southern fringe of the Scavenger Lands. As a mortal, he conjured minor demons the lord of his homeland. One day, a summoning went wrong. The rampaging demon drained all the color from Snow, and left his wife pregnant. She died giving birth to a demonblooded daughter. Snow raised the child as his own, and she continued to follow him after he exalted as a Twilight. While this character primarily focused on Sorcery (this is where I fell in love with summoning), he also was quite proficient at Snake Style. He joined up with the Circle some time after Ellario vanished and continued with them to the end of their adventure. Along the way there were a few complications, notably when a censor of Yu-Shan called in a favor with the group's Eclipse to have Snow's daughter killed. The assassination when wrong, and she survived. When Snow learned of the party's betrayal and how extensive the conspiracy had been, he attempted to summon the Heart of Darkness to swallow recently reconquered Thorns. Luckily, he hadn't quite mastered that Spell yet so the city was spared his wrath until cooler heads could prevail. They worked out a new deal with the powers than be in Yu-Shan. Through some rigorous work, the daughter's essence was purified of the demon-taint and she transformed into a minor god rather than the demon they feared she would become. She got a gig as the Goddess of Exorcisms after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:38:35-08:00","id":1354657,"title":"","content":"My first characters was a Dawn caste. Didn't know much about exalted. I think he secretly worked for the Realm agent in Cherak. Don't remember a lot about him.<br /> <br /> My 2nd character was a straight up doob casting sorcerer that was always on the run from the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:38:40-08:00","id":1354658,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't remember my first Exalted characters (I remember my first Werewolf: The Apocalypse character... and that's about it for &quot;first&quot; characters... oh and my first Force and Destiny character because I'm still playing him). My first characters just weren't that interesting.<br /> <br /> The 2E characters which stuck with me aren't really suitable for 3E. Like my Essence 10 Infernal, The Prince of Iron and Fire who eventually became the new Unconquered Sun. Or Ganan Malfisto, a Dragon-Blooded who took part in the Usurpation and survived through to present day in order to hang-out with a Circle of Celestials.<br /> <br /> Except for Cynis Anade, an Air Aspect Dynast whom I've reimagined as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341506-dynasty-of-dovak-campaign-notes-and-play-report\">Cynis Ganan</a>. He's basically 99% the same character. Big guy. Big hammer. Occult genius. Anade had a lot more summoned Neomah... but yeah. It's been a blast dusting that old chestnut off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-13-2019, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:39:04-08:00","id":1354659,"title":"","content":"I didn't know anything about Exalted when I first started playing. I sat in for a session, listened in and went &quot;Oh! how about that throway NPC! I could play him!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Storyteller tried to dissuade me &quot;Exalted isn't....a balanced system. You're playing with high-essence Solars...&quot; I just assumed he was metagaming and min/maxing, so I went ahead with it.......and tried to play a Dragon King Archer. Because I'd played an Arcane Archer in Baulder's Gate on xbox and that was neat!<br /> <br /> Not a Dragon-blood. A Dragon King. Who wouldn't want to play a rad dinosaur!?<br /> <br /> The Storyteller....uh....took my sheet and inserted some *blatantly illegal* abilities in there to try to at least balance the scales a tiny bit.<br /> <br /> It...it really didn't work out at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:39:50-08:00","id":1354660,"title":"","content":"Well my first character was a twilight sorcerer with sorcery focus who, in the first session, was ambushed while sleeping by a pack of roaming zombies, then proceeded to drop the Flight of the Brilliant Raptor he was attempting to cast, and thereafter gained a crippling fear of zombies. He thankfully started the game with Adamant Skin Technique which he abused constantly to do anything from jump down from a high height to walking through death traps so he didn\u2019t have to solve them. He also helped another twilight give the Realm an ultimatum to surrender or be destroyed, and then when they declined started chucking unstable PSVs into the cities. I think shortly after that the other twilight became the new emperor and my character just fucked off to go build manses. I liked him, but he was not my best character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:53:20-08:00","id":1354663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1354653-who-were-your-first-characters?p=1354658#post1354658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2E characters which stuck with me aren't really suitable for 3E. Like my Essence 10 Infernal</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to ask why the character wouldn't be suitable for 3E, then I saw Essence 10 Infernal. Did you start out at Essence 10, or did you actually have to work to get there? I think Essence 6 (also an Infernal) was the highest I've ever hit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a Dragon-blood. A Dragon King. Who wouldn't want to play a rad dinosaur!?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember right, we had a Pterok NPC that occasionally helped us out in that first game I was in. The Dragon Kings can be pretty sweet and for a one-off throwaway character, I imagined it'd be a fairly unique experience. Of course, my groups tend to go for mixed parties, balance be damned. We're less concerned about being equal in power among ourselves and more interested in having diverse powers and abilities, whatever form those take. As ST, I mainly tweak experience costs as our sole concession to balance concerns. But for a one-off character that wouldn't be an issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:58:11-08:00","id":1354664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1354653-who-were-your-first-characters?p=1354660#post1354660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> think shortly after that the other twilight became the new emperor and my character just fucked off to go build manses. I liked him, but he was not my best character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Snow did a lot of manse-building in his later days as well. I got the spell to raises manses in a hurry so I was giving those things out to everyone in the party. In the session leading up to our assault on the Imperial Manse, I had just finished a manse for our Dawn, receiving a minor Hearthstone from the manse in exchange. The ST said I could pick any 1-dot stone in the book. I got the one that lets you navigate mazes. The next session, the ST describes the labyrinth we encounter as soon as we entered the manse. I just held up my hearthstone and say &quot;We go that way.&quot; The ST just frowned and tore out at least 5 pages from his notebook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T14:10:30-08:00","id":1354668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1354653-who-were-your-first-characters?p=1354663#post1354663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was about to ask why the character wouldn't be suitable for 3E, then I saw Essence 10 Infernal. Did you start out at Essence 10, or did you actually have to work to get there? I think Essence 6 (also an Infernal) was the highest I've ever hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>We started as a mixed Solaroid Circle of normal PCs, but a few sessions in we time-skipped up to Essence 8 (and retired an Abyssal for a Lunar). We played that basically weekly for three years. I still have the sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T14:21:46-08:00","id":1354670,"title":"","content":"I got started with 3e, with my Dawn Symphony of Broken Chains, which was more or less me trying to make a paladin-ish sort of guy inspired by King Arthur, Artoria from Fate and Knight Artorias from Dark Souls (the latter, in that he was missing an arm and had that whole &quot;missing arm but still wearing armor gauntlet&quot; aesthetic). Second was Fang of the Temperate Dragon, another Dawn who was obsessed with enlightenment and pursuing all paths of external power (Sorcery, Martial Arts, Evocations). Both were kind of experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T14:26:35-08:00","id":1354671,"title":"","content":"My first character was Fate-Thwarting Falcon, a War Supernal Zenith who was retconned into an Integrity Supernal after the game turned out to be about Nexus Intrigue.<br /> <br /> All the players were new except the ST, so when I became the first player to hit Limit Break, the ST offered to play out my Limit Break to give me and the rest of the group a feel for what a Limit Break was like.<br /> <br /> Accepting was a <b>fatal</b> mistake. Within a few hours of playing my character, the ST managed to set all of Nexus aflame and start a bloody civil war with innocent casualties in the thousands, using my Zenith's Presence to convince the rest of the Circle to help. The whole Circle was goody 2 shoes, so that was a hell of a departure from our characters' normal actions.<br /> <br /> That session was hilarious and memorable, but afterwards we had pretty much destroyed everything the group had built up to that point so the game just died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T15:36:26-08:00","id":1354683,"title":"","content":"My first character was a Dawn Caste named Chen Minxia, way back in the summer of 2001 (Good God).<br /> <br /> She was one of the Hundred Riders of the Demon, a mysterious supernatural master whose nature I never did quite find out. Taken into service as a child, she trained as a warrior, plundered villages and made off with slaves for the Demon...until one day the Riders attacked a caravan and a Dragon-Blooded Sorcerer among them fought back. Chen charged the Sorcerer as her fellows fell beneath his Death of Obsidian Butterflies. A peerless swordmaster, she matched the Exalt blow by blow until the Sun came, caught her up in a suspended moment of time and told her &quot;Preserve the innocent by cutting out the wicked&quot;. <br /> <br /> Newly Exalted, she didn't kill the Dragon-Blooded and ended up saving him from the other surviving Riders, leading to a memorable chase scene where she eventually met up with a Solar Circle made up of a Night Caste...and three other Dawn Castes. Yes, four Dawns and one Night in one Circle. <br /> <br /> Our campaign rode harder than the Lord of the Rings and included such memorable moments as us needing to board an airship so we put one of our Dawns in a catapault, shot him up to it so he could knock the ship out of the sky, so we could get onto it. Chen's finest moment came when a corrupt Elemental Dragon Censor came after our circle with a surprise attack of spirits. As the only one with any Occult, Chen had learned Ghost-Eating and I'd just assembled my first Combo with it. And instead of fighting a holding action to keep the dragon at bay while the other Dawns rampaged through the dragon's forces, she single-handedly ganked it in the first round while burning 60 motes of essence in an all-or-nothing attack that paid off with buckets of successes. <br /> <br /> I've played many rpgs in my life but I've never loved a game like I love Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11870-epiphany","name":"Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T18:47:47-08:00","id":1354706,"title":"","content":"My first Solar was named Shichirou, the bastard son of an Orgiastic Fugitive Dragon-Blooded. He was a vainglorious brawler who decided to stand and fight against some zombies in Thorns and took his Second Breath as a result. He didn\u2019t do it to save a bunch of people, per se, but rather because those survivors would think he was awesome.<br /> <br /> Then one player in the group made a character that could reliably make five-dot artifacts in some ridiculously short span of time, and from there the game turned into a bizarre and at times gruesome arms-race between ST and players, culminating in multi-hour arguments and an explosive Essence 8 finale when the ST quit after I punched off half the Ebon Dragon\u2019s health bar in a single turn.<br /> <br /> Not great.<br /> <br /> My first Abyssal was named Son-of-Void Dragon, the game fell on its face right out of the gate so I only played him for one or two sessions. <br /> <br /> My first Lunar was an albatross-totem in 2e. That game sadly didn\u2019t really take off either.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t played any other splat except as an ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T20:23:34-08:00","id":1354712,"title":"","content":"My first character was Seeker of Vengeance, a Dusk Caste. He had been killed in what he thought was supposed to be a nonlethal duel, by a guy who he thought was his <i>friendly</i> rival. He wasn't very happy about it. I honestly forget all the details of the game, but I do recall we had two Abyssals, several Solars, and eventually a Dragon-Blood hanging around.<br /> <br /> Poor Seeker got into a fight with the Circle's mostly-friendly Sidereal ally, which was when I (as a fairly new player) learned all about Violet Bier of Sorrows Style in some detail.<br /> <br /> The most memorable event from my perspective, though, was when the other Abyssal, Purest Ash (I think he was a Day Caste?), summoned the ghost of a powerful Dragon-Blood and then managed to botch his binding roll on like 10 dice. He ended up with the ghost possessing him for a while, a truly ignominious fate for a deathknight.<br /> <br /> I don't recall exactly how long ago this was, but it was back in the 1e days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T01:54:57-08:00","id":1354735,"title":"","content":"My first character was Iselsi Amun Varl, who pretended to be Nellens Ravere, a merchant who was really a spy. I gave him Breeding 5 (because come on, it was 2nd ed DBs! Those tasty motes). Which... is a bit ridiculous for a Nellens, but I didn't realise that at the time.<br /> <br /> He adventured around the West with his sworn brotherhood, and even Yu-Shan, but when he took them to Lookshy to rescue a young Pelleps woman, they discovered it was his daughter, and then that he was an Iselsi, and then that he'd been spying on them the whole time for the Empress, so he had to jump in the sea and escape sharpish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T13:39:43-08:00","id":1354812,"title":"","content":"My first Exalted character (2e), from back before I really had any idea what was going on with the system or setting, was a bog-standard Twilight sorcerer/doctor/lore-monkey. He was hampered by a GM who was stingy with Lore checks and a total lack of understanding of how to make sorcery work. The Traveling Scholar of Sovereign Chains really only stands out in my mind for having preposterously over-the-top descriptions of channeling magic, mostly because I was really bored in combat.<br /> <br /> My first 3e character, and also the first I actually understood, was Herald of the Endless Road-- a Dawn Caste courier and Brawl Supernal. He was solomn, composed, utterly implacable, loyal to his friends, ruthless as hell to his enemies, and somewhat ashamed of his skill set-- he was good at reading, manipulating, and killing people, none of which he was terribly happy about. (Major Intimacy: I'm Not Good at Good Things). He was a lot of fun; unfortunately, the campaign died with him still sitting in prison in Yu-Shon for executing a defeated foe. <br /> <br /> (In his defense, we had WAY too many npcs scheming against us).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T17:10:25-08:00","id":1354834,"title":"","content":"I joined my friend's campaign around session 4 or 5 so they all had a good dynamic already. This was 2e, but in 3e terms you'd have a Volfer/Cloud Strife type, a Resistance/Armor supernal, a Sorcerer Pirate Queen, and a Stealth Archer. <br /> <br /> So a group of super great fighters. <br /> <br /> My first character therefore was a complete noncombatant. Mako Li (real name: Wu Sheng-Tong) of the Lesser House Wu was an Eclipse caste who Exalted upon meeting the Mask of Winters on a secret expedition to be his merchant back-channel to the Great Isle. Mako was one of those House Members who didn't get the gift of the dragons. <br /> <br /> After panicking from sheer dread upon seeing the Mask, he embarrassed his older brother by fleeing the room. Mako's brother loudly berated him and was about to kill him when Mako's Exaltation arrived and he turned his brother's blade back on himself with a single flick of his folding fan. <br /> <br /> Mechanically, all Socialise, Linguistics, Presence, and a splash of Integrity to flavor. He had Conviction 5 Valor 1 Empathy 2 and Temperance 4, I think. <br /> <br /> He didn't learn a combat or defense charm for a literal real life year, probably around Essence 3 or 4. Then he decided to become the real heartless bastard everyone thought he was, picked up some Ebon Dragon Charms (Hollow Heart Transcendence) and a Sidereal Martial Art (Charcoal March of Spiders), and a Fae charm just for good measure (Bastion of the Self: Heart). <br /> <br /> He was a massive dick, manipulative, heartless, and cruel, but there was always the sense that he was the party's heartless cruel dick, and they had kind of a dread fascination with watching him use other people to get what the party needed. For a season he was even in the court of the Wyld Hunt Shogun, always making it look like he was helping out on paper but actually miring them down with bureaucracy and logistical hold ups","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T10:03:28-08:00","id":1354896,"title":"","content":"My first Exalted character? Hmmm. I was a Sidereal, and it was late 1st edition. We played for like 4 or 5 sessions before real life got in the way and the ST stopped running games. I don't recall much about him other than he used throw, duck fate is perfect for scouting, and reducing target numbers is really powerful. <br /> <br /> In Second edition my first character I think was a green haired ugly crafter who enjoyed tinkering with life and altering other living creatures for fun. Lots and lots of crafting charms. pet tiger for a bodyguard. abused his allies for his own benefit. Mostly a dick but some really fun and funny moments in our group. Mostly from being a jerk to his team and sometimes being a jerk to enemies. <br /> <br /> My favorite second edition character was a lovable dumb but charming ex pitfighter who really played up the omni-tactical battle hydra roll. The Power club from Mountain folk allowed archery and melee, then Solar MA (Brawl in third). Never really used throw but I had cascade of cutting whatever-I-throw. Oh, and he had the speak all languages stone so the party was forced to use his translations in several situations. All to great comedic effect. <br /> <br /> I'll be running my third 3rd edition game later today but I haven't really made a npc that has joined the party yet. Only my 1st edition character wasn't a GMNPC who joined the party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:59:57-08:00","id":1355672,"title":"","content":"Nalia was my 1e Dawn, a pirate captain and abolitionist.<br /> She fell victim to the Dawn Caste problem where I ended up investing in brawl, dodge, melee and archery and ended up passable in several combat fields rather than great at any of them. She turned out to be a shockingly good performer though.<br /> <br /> I've played other versions of her since now that I understand the formula.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T22:25:22-08:00","id":1355769,"title":"","content":"2.5 character in a play by post game- Bridges the Sun and Moon. Bridget was the first name I came up with, then I extrapolated a more thematic name from there, but we stuck with Bridget most of the time anyways. Totally new to the system, never heard of it, hadn't read anything when I started chargen so it was mostly me trying to recreate a high-level Pathfinder character. <br /> We eventually settled on a Twilight with some good craft, athletics, and resistance charms. Her and her family were Wyld mutants/blacksmiths (large, unsettling voice, ugly, third eye) who lived in a remote mountains area, controlling bridges in exchange for fees like livestock- basically bridge troll mountain smiths. When the Guild tried to break up their little troll toll on the bridges in the area, she fought back, exalted, and in the process of fighting off their sorcerer she eventually liberated a slave plantation. <br /> <br /> That all being backstory, the actual game involved a circle coincidentally all arriving in the same flying castle, each with their own goals- Bridget was mad that it passed through her territory without the proper tithe of three sheep and a night of ritual to detect and ward off the fey. Eventually this led to a wild night trying to protect a town from an attack by a cult, before everything in a 50 mile radius got accidentally blasted into Malfeas. The rest of the game was us trying to manage the villagers lives in hell, although that got a bit messy for various reasons. <br /> <br /> Overall a great introduction to the system and a great New character who really can into her own after being adapted from Pathfinder!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25854-santova","name":"Santova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}